<Input><Text-field style="Maple Input" layout="Normal"># 6. Derive, rather than insert, the two coefficients.
# t is arbitrary, xi has coefficient vector V C t, z1=t1-t4, z2=t2-t5.
# Qc represents q(Ct). Its first two rows/columns determine H if
# Qc = transpose(DzMap) H DzMap; check the WHOLE identity.
# Maple reserves D for differential operators; do not assign to or unprotect D.
DzMap := Matrix([[1,0,0,-1,0],[0,1,0,0,-1]]):
CheckMatrix(DzMap . Pavg,&quot;DzMap P = 0, so z1,z2 are unchanged by I-P&quot;):
Qc := map(factor,LinearAlgebra:-Transpose(C) . B . C):
H := Qc[1..2,1..2]:
CheckMatrix(Qc-LinearAlgebra:-Transpose(DzMap) . H . DzMap,
            &quot;q(Ct) depends only on z1,z2 through H&quot;):
CheckZero(H[1,1]-H[2,2],&quot;equal diagonal entries of H&quot;):
CheckZero(H[1,2]-H[2,1],&quot;symmetric off-diagonal entries of H&quot;):
dN := factor(H[1,1]):
eN := factor(H[1,2]):
AN := factor((dN+eN)/2):
BN := factor((dN-eN)/2):
<Font encoding="UTF-8">printf(&quot;DERIVED d_N, e_N, A_N, B_N (in this order):\134n&quot;):
</Font>print(dN,eN,AN,BN);

# Only now compare the derived answers with the manuscript's proposed formulas.
CheckZero(AN-(N-4)*(2*N^2-9*N+8)/18,&quot;A_N formula&quot;):
CheckZero(BN-(N-4)*(2*N^2-7*N+4)/2,&quot;B_N formula&quot;):
<Font encoding="UTF-8">printf(&quot;PASS: both displayed formulas follow from the contraction.\134n&quot;):
</Font>
# z1bar,z2bar are independent formal symbols standing for complex conjugates.
# This avoids assumptions about conjugate(N) and checks a polynomial identity.
q_z := expand(dN*(z1*z1bar+z2*z2bar)+eN*(z1bar*z2+z2bar*z1)):
